	(text "Radio pod (spec 2b): the bay board of a cable-free key module, and the hub's receiver on the hub-radio carrier. Radio only: 3.3 V and 5 V come in over the lead\n(J2, JST GH, 1:1 to pod-power: 1 +5V, 2 GND, 3 EN_5V, 4 VBAT_SENSE, 5 GND, 6 +3V3) and go on into the key board through J1 (pins as the port board, spec 1).\nU1 MDBT50Q-1MV2: VDD = VDDH = 3.3 V (normal-voltage mode, DCCH open; the REG1 DC/DC inductor and the 32 MHz crystal are inside the module).\nSPI on pins that are not 'low frequency I/O only'; SCK and MOSI through 33 R at the source. CS and INT: 100 k pull-ups (INT is open drain on the expander).\nLED data: 74AHCT1G125 on the 5 V pins (VIH 2 V), enable tied low, 100 R at its output (the key board has 220 R before LED1), 100 k pull-down at its input.\nBay pin 6 (SPARE) reads low on the hub carrier and floats on a key board: internal pull-up, read once at start; 1 k in series, so a driven pin cannot short into the carrier's GND.\nUSB-C J3 is the module's own USB for flashing and a console: VBUS feeds only the nRF52840's USB regulator pin (2.2 R + 10 uF), never the 3.3 V rail,\nso the pod must be powered (lead or hub) to be flashed. 27 R in D+ / D- as Raytac's reference circuit; Rd 5.1 k on CC1 / CC2; USBLC6-2 at the receptacle.\nJ4: 2x5 1.27 mm Cortex debug pinout (1 VTref, 2 SWDIO, 4 SWDCLK, 6 SWO = P1.00, 10 nRESET). Y1 with 12 pF as Raytac's reference circuit (crystal CL 9 pF).\nThe two M2 holes are board features (placement script), as on the port board. Pin map for the firmware: firmware/pod-pinmap.json."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 269.24 0)
